      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-01-14T00:39:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Amazian\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/aeb1de/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Amazian:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If it requires money and the power to keep things to myself, that works.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>During each of the three Kickstarters, there was an option to pay a certain amount to become a playtest, with the status of playtester carrying through to successive expansions, and even to the not-yet-announced new game.</p>\n<p>I have never seen an option outside of the Kickstarters that allows one to become a playtester. If you're gung ho, you might try emailing Christopher: <a href=\"mailto:christopher@greaterthangames.com\">christopher@greaterthangames.com</a></p>",
      "post_number": 2,
